{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/952744-wielding-two-weapons","id":952744,"title":"Wielding two weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-17T14:36:01-07:00","id":952744,"title":"Wielding two weapons","content":"Hello, one thing that is mentioned a couple of times is wielding two weapons but there seem to be no real rules for it that I can see, obviously if there is please point them out. There is the ambidextrous merit in god machine and it mentions in the initiative wielding a weapon in both hands you get increased penatly to initiative.<br /> <br /> What benefit does wielding two weapons yield? I mean apart from looking cool can you actually do anything with them, like make an off hand attack because if not seems rather pointless taking an initiative penatly to look cool.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:21:02-07:00","id":952781,"title":"","content":"Pretty much the only advantage of wielding two weapons is that both of your hands have weapons in them. If someone disarms you or causes Arm Wrack on one of your hands, the other hand is still armed and functional. If one of the weapons is a shield you can attack with the other weapon and still get the Concealed benefit from the shield. If one is a melee weapon and the other is a firearm you can switch between shooting and swashbuckling without having to waste turns switching weapons. But no, you can't like attack twice in one turn or anything. In 1e there was a two-weapon fighting style that expanded what you could do with dual-wielding. In 2e, there isn't such a Merit yet, but the upcoming book Hurt Locker probably will have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-17-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:59:28-07:00","id":952805,"title":"","content":"It does. You can find the list of Hurt Locker Fighting Styles here - <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/</a> The second and fourth dots are pretty nice. not sure about the other two.<br /> <br /> EDIT - do a search for Ambidex if youw ant to jump right to Two Weapon Fighting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:07:46-07:00","id":952814,"title":"","content":"Though, we don't know if that's still what it will look like in the final draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpa